    "story": "When the Private Network Gateway is not an option, serverless compute can still reach resources in the customer's VPC and on-premises over AWS PrivateLink. A private endpoint rule in the workspace's Network Connectivity Configuration (NCC) connects to a VPC endpoint service in the customer's shared services VPC. The endpoint service fronts a Network Load Balancer whose listeners map dedicated ports (e.g. 1521, 3306) to target groups; targets are IPs in the VPC or on-premises, reached through the Transit Gateway and Direct Connect / Site-to-Site VPN. The workspace VPC is attached to the same Transit Gateway and is not on the serverless path. The customer provisions and maintains the NLB, and adds a listener and target group for every new target.",
